          "id": "fe805c98f11c676b2b821ca8583fb296a739cd48",
          "message": "docs(security): take repo-template's security policy, with the disclosure process and timelines (#689)\n\nScorecard scores this repository 4/10 on Security-Policy: \"security policy file\ndetected: Warn: no linked content found\". The file exists - all twelve affected\nrepositories carry the same 735-byte stub - but Scorecard also grades its\nCONTENT, and the stub has no links, no addresses and no concrete timelines, so\nit reads as a placeholder rather than a policy someone could act on.\n\nrepo-template's version is the one that scores: it names the private advisory\nURL for this repository, links GitHub's own guidance on private reporting, and\nreplaces \"we will acknowledge within 48 hours\" with a table that commits to\nassessment and fix windows by severity - explicitly scoped to what a\nsingle-maintainer project can actually meet. It also documents the disclosure\nprocess end to end (report, triage, private fork, release, publish + CVE) and\nsays reporters are credited.\n\nThe {{GITHUB_REPO_URL}} placeholder is substituted for this repository, so the\nadvisory link is real rather than pointing at the template.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
